{
  "name": "l0_switchable_light",
  "about": "CLight (vampire.dll; `walks/L0-r012.md`): the switchable light's startup and transitions. KeyValue 0x101303c0: a `pitch` key replaces only X of the angles (GetAngles slot 221, atof, SetAbsAngles slot 218) and is applied in lump order, after the `angles` key every shipped light authors first, so `spot` (angles 0 0 0, pitch -30) stands at m_angAbsRotation.x = -30. Spawn 0x10130460: an UNNAMED light (`m_iName == 0`, 0x10130463) is removed through UTIL_RemoveImmediate 0x1000e255 -> 0x101cd970 with no floor and no publish; a named one floors `fade_time` to the literal 0.05 at 0x10453b74 (0x1013047e) -- the style-7 `dim` too, which then publishes nothing (0x101304aa); START_OFF publishes \"a\" (0x101304c7) and OVERWRITES the authored \"bcd\" with \"a\"; an authored pattern publishes as is (0x10130502); none, or `pattern \"\"` (NULL through AllocPooledString 0x1042bff0), publishes \"m\" and stores \"m\" (0x10130518). Use 0x10130580 (slot 173, driven by `entity_call Use`): style < 32 does nothing; else ShouldToggle 0x100a98f0 on the START_OFF bit -- OFF on an off light and ON on an on light refuse, SET and TOGGLE always toggle -- then Toggle 0x101306f0: TurnOn 0x10130610 publishes \"m\" because the pattern is now \"a\" (0x10130622), TurnOff 0x10130690 publishes \"a\" (0x101306a7). InputSetPattern 0x10130780 (row 6, FIELD_STRING): stores and publishes \"abc\" (0x101307bd) and clears START_OFF; the `TurnOn` INPUT (0x10130720, which bypasses Use) then publishes \"m\" (leading 'a'); a USE_ON on the lit light publishes nothing; the `Use` INPUT arrives as USE_TOGGLE (CBaseEntity::InputUse 0x100ac9f0) and turns it off; a parameterless SetPattern is a NULL string (variant_t::Convert 0x100d05d0 VOID -> STRING) that stores NULL and publishes \"\"; a float parameter is refused by AcceptInput 0x100abc90 before the function runs. InputFadeToPattern 0x10130800 (row 7) from `lamp`'s \"m\" to \"pq\": cur = 'm' (109), tgt = 'p' (112), the pattern stored, FadeThink 0x101308d0 installed (ThinkSet 0x100ac4e0) and due now, nothing published synchronously; the next dispatcher pass publishes \"n\" (0x1013094b), then \"o\" one fade_time (0.05, the floor) later, then the whole \"pq\" at cur == tgt (0x1013091b) with m_flNextThink = 0 (the dispatcher's no-think, 0x10033e59). ScriptHide 0x101305d0 is TurnOff first (\"a\"). Kill 0x101306d0 is TurnOff first (\"a\", START_OFF set) then CBaseEntity::Kill 0x100acf90, for a hidden light too, and the light leaves the world. Reported as `fail`, a published pattern, a stored word or a site payload differs from retail's.",
  "stage": "arena",
  "seed": 1,
