  "notes": "The lights spawn through `spawn` actions at 0.02 rather than as `rows`: zero is the stage's Activate, and a row's Spawn runs in Load, before the recording window, so a Spawn-time site is observable only on a runtime spawn (as `l0_ambient_init` does). Timing: the arena runs at 60 Hz; an input fires in its frame and a think on the next pass, so each publish is given a frame of slack. Retail's dispatcher (0x10033de0) fires a think up to one frametime early and rebinds curtime to the think time; the port's fires at or after it, so the fade steps may land one frame later than retail's -- the `within` bounds tolerate that. The nameless light has no targetname, so its sites are matched with an empty `who` and its style (35); it is dead before the runner's first sweep, so it has no `removed`. The `killed` light's `removed` is the runner's own between-frames kind."
